; Find the closed holder of an object
;
; Climbs the holder chain of the record in IX: takes its holder, and while that
; holder has flag bit 5 or 3 set (active/open/alive, or dead/disabled: not a
; shut container), continues with the holder's own holder. Stops at a holder
; with neither bit and returns its id, or returns $FF when the chain reaches
; a location. IX is kept.
;
; IX Record of the object or actor
; O:A Id of the closed holder, $FF when none
@label=FindClosedHolder
c$9E7A PUSH IX
*$9E7C LD A,(IX+$01)
@isub=CP AT_LOCATION
 $9E7F CP $FF
 $9E81 JR Z,$9E92
 $9E83 EX AF,AF'        ; keep the holder id
 $9E84 LD A,(IX+$01)
 $9E87 CALL $9BCA
 $9E8A LD A,(IX+$07)
 $9E8D AND $28          ; bits 5 and 3: active/open/alive, dead/disabled
 $9E8F JR NZ,$9E7C
 $9E91 EX AF,AF'
*$9E92 POP IX
 $9E94 RET
